event: step.delta
data: {"index":0,"delta":{"content":{"text":"**Initiating the Analysis**\n\nI've initiated the analysis phase and identified the core topic: proving that the sum of the first *n* positive odd integers equals *n* squared using induction. This is the foundation upon which I'm building, and my focus is now shifting to creating the inductive proof.\n\n\n","type":"text"},"type":"thought_summary"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

event: step.delta
data: {"index":0,"delta":{"content":{"text":"**Interpreting the Geometry**\n\nI'm now integrating the geometric understanding to complement the induction proof. I'm visualizing the construction of an $n \\times n$ square using successive $L$-shaped layers, each adding the next odd integer. The base case starts with a $1 \\times 1$ square, and each gnomon incrementally extends the square, directly illustrating the summation. I am aiming to illustrate the gnomon.\n\n\n","type":"text"},"type":"thought_summary"},"event_type":"step.delta"}

